[' To create a flexible user retrieval service in C# with the given considerations, we'll utilize Entity Framework Core (EF Core) to interact with our distributed database system. Below is an outline of the necessary components and their implementation:

1. **Database Context**: Create a database context class that encapsulates our EF Core DbContext and implements Dependency Injection for seamless scaling.

```csharp
public interface IDatabaseContext
{
    DbSet<User> Users { get; set; }
}

public class DatabaseContext : Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContext, IDatabaseContext
{
    public DatabaseContext(DbContextOptions<DatabaseContext> options) : base(options) { }
    public virtual DbSet<User> Users { get; set; }
}
```

2. **QueryBuilder**: Design a QueryBuilder class to construct SQL queries based on filter criteria provided as a dictionary.

```csharp
public class QueryBuilder
{
    private readonly string _tableName;
    private StringBuilder _sql = new StringBuilder();

    public QueryBuilder(string tableName)
    {
        _tableName = tableName;
    }

    public void AddFilter(string column, Operator operatorType, object value)
    {
        if (_sql.Length > 0)
            _sql.Append(" AND ");

        _sql.Append($"{column} {operatorType.GetEnumName()} @{column}");
    }

    public string BuildQuery(IDictionary<string, object> filters)
    {
        if (filters != null && filters.Any())
        {
            _sql.Append(" WHERE ");
            foreach (var filter in filters)
                AddFilter(filter.Key, filter.Value.GetType().Name.ToLower() switch
                {
                    "int" => Operator.Equal,
                    "string" => Operator.Contains,
                    _ => throw new NotSupportedException($"Operator not supported for type '{filter.Value.GetType().FullName}'")
                }, filter.Value);
        }

        return $"SELECT * FROM {_tableName} {_sql}";
    }
}
```

3. **Operator Enum**: Define an Operator enum to support different SQL comparison operators.

```csharp
public enum Operator
{
    Equal,
    NotEqual,
    GreaterThan,
    LessThan,
    GreaterThanOrEqual,
    LessThanOrEqual,
    Contains,
    Like
}
```

4. **User Retrieval Service**: Implement the UserRetrievalService class that manages query construction and execution using the above components.

```csharp
public interface IUserRetrievalService
{
    IDataReader ExecuteQuery(IDictionary<string, object> filters);
}

public class UserRetrievalService : IUserRetrievalService
{
    private readonly IDatabaseContext _context;

    public UserRetrievalService(IDatabaseContext context)
    {
        _context = context;
    }

    public IDataReader ExecuteQuery(IDictionary<string, object> filters)
    {
        var queryBuilder = new QueryBuilder("Users");
        queryBuilder.BuildQuery(filters);
        return _context.Database.ExecuteSqlRaw(queryBuilder.BuildQuery(filters), filters).CreateDataReader();
    }
}
```

By implementing this UserRetrievalService, we have successfully created a flexible user retrieval service in C# that meets the provided requirements. Further enhancements can be made for better query optimization, caching, and concurrency management.']

