void create_and_populate_list(uint32_t n, uint32_t* rxtags, uint32_t* rtis, void(*process)(data_item*)) {
    data_item** list = (data_item**)malloc(n * sizeof(data_item*));
    if (!list) return;

    pthread_t threads[n];
    uint32_t chunk_size = n / 10;
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        uint32_t* data = &rxtags[i * chunk_size];
        data[1] = rtis[i * chunk_size];
        pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, create_and_populate, data);
    }

    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        pthread_join(threads[i], (void**)&list[i]);
        if (list[i]) process(list[i]);
    }

    free(list);
}
```

This code provides a basic structure for creating and populating a list of `data_item` structures. Each data item contains an NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T structure, uniquely identified by a combination of RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG and RNTI. The function dynamically creates the list in chunks to improve performance in a multi-threaded environment.

The `create_and_populate` function is designed to be executed asynchronously on separate threads, with each thread creating a data item, populating its PDU structure, and performing any necessary hash verification. This allows for concurrent operations and handling high volumes of data.

Error handling is not explicitly implemented in this example but can be added by checking return values from memory allocation functions (`malloc`, `pthread_create`, etc.) and modifying the code as needed.']

